From f5b629b6640d7e7519ac2d41e6d6b8161c31d147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 01:33:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 203/638] web_applications: enable settings navigation on AROS
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement:
Chrome's generic desktop command controller offers Web App settings on AROS, but the navigation implementation and chrome://app-settings URL contract were hidden behind a fixed desktop OS list.

Decision:
Admit AROS to the existing Web App settings declarations, implementation, URL constants, and internal-host registry. The path remains native Chrome navigation with its existing UMA entry-point accounting.

Evidence:
chrome_pages.o, webui_url_constants.o, and browser_command_controller.o compile successfully in out/aros-chrome.

Chain:
 first native Chromium window; compile blocker from full Chrome resume 19.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc    | 4 ++--
 chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.h     | 4 ++--
 chrome/common/webui_url_constants.cc | 5 +++--
 chrome/common/webui_url_constants.h  | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc
index 580ecdf01a..3a644088e6 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/chrome_pages.cc
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 #endif
 
